    "description": "### Business Context\nPostmates City Operations is monitoring marketplace reliability. Write a query to compute the daily cancellation rate for all on-demand dispatches requested between **'2024-06-01' and '2024-06-03'** inclusive, considering only **unbanned clients and unbanned couriers**.\n\n### Metric Formulas & Rules\n- Trips where either the client OR the courier is banned (`banned = 'Yes'`) **must be completely excluded** from both the numerator and denominator.\n- Trips with `status` in (`'cancelled_by_driver'`, `'cancelled_by_client'`) are considered cancelled. Trips with status `'completed'` are not cancelled.\n- **`cancellation_rate`**: Calculated as `Total Cancelled Trips / Total Requested Trips`, rounded to **2 decimal places**.\n- Output columns: `request_date`, `cancellation_rate`.\n- Sort by `request_date` ASC.\n\n### Input Schema\n**users** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `banned` (VARCHAR: 'Yes', 'No')\n- `role` (VARCHAR: 'client', 'driver')\n\n**trips** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `client_id` (INT)\n- `driver_id` (INT)\n- `status` (VARCHAR: 'completed', 'cancelled_by_driver', 'cancelled_by_client')\n- `request_date` (DATE)",
    "schemaSql": "\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  banned VARCHAR(5),\n  role VARCHAR(10)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE trips (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  client_id INT,\n  driver_id INT,\n  status VARCHAR(30),\n  request_date DATE\n);\n\nINSERT INTO users VALUES\n(1, 'No', 'client'),\n(2, 'Yes', 'client'),\n(3, 'No', 'client'),\n(4, 'No', 'client'),\n(10, 'No', 'driver'),\n(11, 'No', 'driver'),\n(12, 'No', 'driver'),\n(13, 'Yes', 'driver');\n\nINSERT INTO trips VALUES\n(1, 1, 10, 'completed', '2024-06-01'),\n(2, 2, 11, 'cancelled_by_driver', '2024-06-01'), -- Client 2 banned -> Exclude\n(3, 3, 12, 'completed', '2024-06-01'),\n(4, 4, 10, 'cancelled_by_client', '2024-06-01'),\n(5, 1, 11, 'completed', '2024-06-02'),\n(6, 3, 10, 'completed', '2024-06-02'),\n(7, 4, 12, 'completed', '2024-06-02'),\n(8, 2, 12, 'completed', '2024-06-03'),           -- Client 2 banned -> Exclude\n(9, 3, 10, 'completed', '2024-06-03'),\n(10, 4, 13, 'cancelled_by_driver', '2024-06-03'), -- Driver 13 banned -> Exclude\n(11, 1, 12, 'cancelled_by_client', '2024-06-03');\n",
