    "orderSensitive": true,
    "description": "### Business Context\nThe Netflix Financial Planning team is tracking subscription revenue across active membership tiers for video streaming plans. A subscription is considered active if `is_active = true` and `auto_renew = true`.\n\nCalculate the **active subscriber count** and **total monthly recurring revenue (MRR)** for each `plan_name`.\n\n### Metric Formulas & Rules\n- Filter for plans where `is_active = true` and `auto_renew = true`.\n- **`active_subscribers`**: Total count of active subscribers on that plan.\n- **`total_mrr`**: Sum of `monthly_fee` for active subscribers, rounded to **2 decimal places**.\n- Output columns: `plan_name`, `active_subscribers`, `total_mrr`.\n- Sort by `total_mrr` DESC, then `plan_name` ASC.\n\n### Input Schema\n**subscriptions** table:\n- `subscription_id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `user_id` (INT)\n- `plan_name` (VARCHAR)\n- `monthly_fee` (NUMERIC)\n- `is_active` (BOOLEAN)\n- `auto_renew` (BOOLEAN)",
    "schemaSql": "\nCREATE TABLE subscriptions (\n  subscription_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  user_id INT,\n  plan_name VARCHAR(50),\n  monthly_fee NUMERIC,\n  is_active BOOLEAN,\n  auto_renew BOOLEAN\n);\n\nINSERT INTO subscriptions VALUES\n(1, 101, 'Premium', 19.99, true, true),\n(2, 102, 'Premium', 19.99, true, false), -- Not auto-renew\n(3, 103, 'Standard', 14.99, true, true),\n(4, 104, 'Standard', 14.99, false, false), -- Inactive\n(5, 105, 'Standard', 14.99, true, true),\n(6, 106, 'Basic', 9.99, true, true),\n(7, 107, 'Premium', 19.99, true, true);\n",
    "starterSql": "-- Netflix: Calculate active subscribers and total MRR by plan_name\n-- Output: plan_name, active_subscribers, total_mrr\nSELECT\n  -- Your code here\nFROM subscriptions;\n",
    "referenceSql": "SELECT \n  plan_name,\n  COUNT(*) AS active_subscribers,\n  ROUND(SUM(monthly_fee), 2) AS total_mrr\nFROM subscriptions\nWHERE is_active = true AND auto_renew = true\nGROUP BY plan_name\nORDER BY total_mrr DESC, plan_name ASC;",
    "expectedColumns": [
      "plan_name",
      "active_subscribers",
      "total_mrr"
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Filter for both `is_active = true` and `auto_renew = true` in the WHERE clause.",
      "Group by `plan_name`.",
      "Order descending by `total_mrr`."
    ],
    "explanation": "### SaaS & Subscription Revenue Metrics\nMRR (Monthly Recurring Revenue) is the single most watched metric in subscription businesses. Filtering out paused or churned accounts before summing is critical to avoid inflating revenue projections."
