    "description": "### Business Context\nThe Stripe Risk & Compliance team needs to flag high-volume merchant accounts. Identify all accounts that have completed **at least 2 successful transactions** and have a **total transaction volume strictly exceeding $1000**.\n\n### Metric Formulas & Rules\n- Only consider transactions with `status = 'completed'`.\n- Filter groups using a `HAVING` clause where:\n  - `COUNT(*) >= 2`\n  - `SUM(amount) > 1000`\n- **`total_volume`**: Sum of transaction amounts, rounded to **2 decimal places**.\n- **`transaction_count`**: Count of completed transactions.\n- Output columns: `merchant_id`, `transaction_count`, `total_volume`.\n- Sort by `total_volume` DESC, then `merchant_id` ASC.\n\n### Input Schema\n**transactions** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `merchant_id` (INT)\n- `amount` (NUMERIC)\n- `status` (VARCHAR: 'completed', 'pending', 'failed')",
    "schemaSql": "\nCREATE TABLE transactions (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  merchant_id INT,\n  amount NUMERIC,\n  status VARCHAR(20)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO transactions VALUES\n(1, 101, 600.00, 'completed'),\n(2, 101, 800.00, 'completed'),  -- Total 1400, count 2 -> Qualifies if thresh <= 1000\n(3, 101, 200.00, 'failed'),\n(4, 102, 3500.00, 'completed'), -- Total 3500, count 1 -> Excluded (needs >= 2)\n(5, 103, 1200.00, 'completed'),\n(6, 103, 900.00, 'completed'),\n(7, 103, 1500.00, 'completed'), -- Total 3600, count 3 -> Qualifies\n(8, 104, 50.00, 'completed'),\n(9, 104, 75.00, 'completed');   -- Total 125, count 2 -> Excluded (volume too low)\n",
    "starterSql": "-- Stripe: Filter merchant accounts by count >= 2 and total volume > 1000\n-- Output: merchant_id, transaction_count, total_volume\nSELECT\n  -- Your code here\nFROM transactions;\n",
    "referenceSql": "SELECT \n  merchant_id,\n  COUNT(*) AS transaction_count,\n  ROUND(SUM(amount), 2) AS total_volume\nFROM transactions\nWHERE status = 'completed'\nGROUP BY merchant_id\nHAVING COUNT(*) >= 2 AND SUM(amount) > 1000\nORDER BY total_volume DESC, merchant_id ASC;",
