    "frequency": "High",
    "category": "Window Functions",
    "orderSensitive": true,
    "description": "### Business Context\nJPMorgan Security & Operations monitors event streams for anomalous rapid repetition. A **Suspicious Burst** occurs when the same `account_id` triggers two consecutive events where:\n1. Both events satisfy `amount >= 500`.\n2. The consecutive event occurs within **300 seconds** of the previous event.\n\n### Metric Formulas & Rules\n- Use `LEAD()` or `LAG()` over `(PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time ASC)`.\n- Filter for consecutive pairs where the elapsed time difference is `<= 300` seconds.\n- **`seconds_apart`**: Calculated as `EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (next_time - event_time))::INT`.\n- Output columns: `account_id`, `t1_id`, `t2_id`, `t1_amount`, `t2_amount`, `seconds_apart`.\n- Sort by `account_id` ASC, `t1_id` ASC.\n\n### Input Schema\n**events** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `account_id` (INT)\n- `amount` (NUMERIC)\n- `event_time` (TIMESTAMP)",
    "schemaSql": "\nCREATE TABLE events (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  account_id INT,\n  amount NUMERIC,\n  event_time TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nINSERT INTO events VALUES\n(1, 1001, 600.00, '2024-06-01 14:00:00'),\n(2, 1001, 750.00, '2024-06-01 14:00:00'::TIMESTAMP + INTERVAL '150 seconds'),\n(3, 1001, 450.00, '2024-06-01 14:05:00'),\n(4, 1002, 600.00, '2024-06-01 15:00:00'),\n(5, 1002, 750.00, '2024-06-01 15:10:00');\n",
    "starterSql": "-- JPMorgan: Detect consecutive events within 300 seconds\n-- Output: account_id, t1_id, t2_id, t1_amount, t2_amount, seconds_apart\nWITH ordered AS (\n  -- Your code here\n)\nSELECT * FROM ordered;\n",
    "referenceSql": "WITH ordered AS (\n  SELECT \n    account_id,\n    id AS t1_id,\n    amount AS t1_amount,\n    event_time,\n    LEAD(id) OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time) AS t2_id,\n    LEAD(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time) AS t2_amount,\n    LEAD(event_time) OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time) AS next_time\n  FROM events\n  WHERE amount >= 500\n)\nSELECT \n  account_id,\n  t1_id,\n  t2_id,\n  t1_amount,\n  t2_amount,\n  EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (next_time - event_time))::INT AS seconds_apart\nFROM ordered\nWHERE t2_id IS NOT NULL \n  AND EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (next_time - event_time)) <= 300\nORDER BY account_id ASC, t1_id ASC;",
    "expectedColumns": [
      "account_id",
      "t1_id",
      "t2_id",
      "t1_amount",
      "t2_amount",
      "seconds_apart"
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Filter `amount >= 500` in the initial CTE so you only evaluate qualified events.",
      "Use `LEAD()` over `(PARTITION BY account ORDER BY event_time)` to inspect the next event timestamp and amount.",
      "Calculate the epoch delta using `EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (next_time - event_time)) <= 300`."
    ],
    "explanation": "### Windowing vs Self-Joins for Fraud\nUsing `LEAD()` scans the dataset linearly in $O(N \\log N)$ time, avoiding an $O(N^2)$ cross self-join that would freeze production databases on high-frequency transaction logs."
