    "description": "### Business Context\nThe Google Ads Marketing Attribution team needs to allocate conversion credit. Under the **First-Touch Attribution Model**, full credit for a user conversion is assigned to the **very first touchpoint interaction** recorded before or during their journey.\n\n### Metric Formulas & Rules\n- Partition touchpoints by `visitor_id` and order by `touch_time ASC`.\n- Use `ROW_NUMBER()` to assign rank `1` to the first interaction.\n- Filter for `rnk = 1`.\n- Output columns: `visitor_id`, `campaign`, `touch_time`.\n- Sort by `visitor_id` ASC.\n\n### Input Schema\n**touchpoints** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `visitor_id` (INT)\n- `campaign` (VARCHAR)\n- `touch_time` (TIMESTAMP)",
    "schemaSql": "\nCREATE TABLE touchpoints (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  visitor_id INT,\n  campaign VARCHAR(50),\n  touch_time TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nINSERT INTO touchpoints VALUES\n(1, 101, 'Organic Search', '2024-05-01 09:00:00'),\n(2, 101, 'Email Campaign', '2024-05-03 14:30:00'),\n(3, 101, 'Retargeting Ad', '2024-05-05 18:15:00'),\n(4, 102, 'Paid Social', '2024-05-02 11:00:00'),\n(5, 102, 'Direct Mail', '2024-05-04 16:00:00');\n",
    "starterSql": "-- Google Ads: Identify first touchpoint using ROW_NUMBER()\n-- Output: visitor_id, campaign, touch_time\nWITH ranked AS (\n  -- Your code here\n)\nSELECT * FROM ranked;\n",
    "referenceSql": "WITH ranked AS (\n  SELECT \n    visitor_id,\n    campaign,\n    touch_time,\n    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (\n      PARTITION BY visitor_id \n      ORDER BY touch_time ASC\n    ) AS rnk\n  FROM touchpoints\n)\nSELECT \n  visitor_id,\n  campaign,\n  touch_time\nFROM ranked\nWHERE rnk = 1\nORDER BY visitor_id ASC;",
    "expectedColumns": [
      "visitor_id",
      "campaign",
      "touch_time"
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Use `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY visitor_id ORDER BY touch_time ASC)`.",
      "Filter for `rnk = 1` in the outer query.",
      "Sort by `visitor_id` ASC."
    ],
    "explanation": "### Attribution Modeling\nFirst-touch and last-touch attribution models are classic product analytics interview questions. Using `ROW_NUMBER()` is deterministic and guarantees exactly one attributed record per user."
