    "description": "### Business Context\nThe DoorDash Compensation & Strategy team needs to find the **exactly 3rd highest Orders** (`orders_fulfilled`) in each `borough_name`. \n\n### Metric Formulas & Rules\n- Do NOT use `LIMIT` or `OFFSET` because each borough must appear in the final report.\n- Use `DENSE_RANK()` partitioned by `borough_id` and ordered by `orders_fulfilled` DESC.\n- Filter strictly for rows where `rnk = 3`.\n- Output columns: `borough_name`, `merchant_name`, `orders_fulfilled`.\n- Sort by `borough_name` ASC, `orders_fulfilled` DESC.\n\n### Input Schema\n**boroughs** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `name` (VARCHAR)\n\n**merchants** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `borough_id` (INT)\n- `name` (VARCHAR)\n- `orders_fulfilled` (INT)",
    "schemaSql": "\nCREATE TABLE boroughs (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name VARCHAR(50)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE merchants (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  borough_id INT,\n  name VARCHAR(50),\n  orders_fulfilled INT\n);\n\nINSERT INTO boroughs VALUES\n(1, 'Group One'),\n(2, 'Group Two');\n\nINSERT INTO merchants VALUES\n(1, 1, 'Alpha Item', 1000), -- Rank 1\n(2, 1, 'Beta Item', 850),   -- Rank 2 (Qualifies if N=2)\n(3, 1, 'Gamma Item', 850),  -- Rank 2 tie (Qualifies if N=2)\n(4, 1, 'Delta Item', 700),  -- Rank 3 (Qualifies if N=3)\n(5, 2, 'Echo Item', 1200),  -- Rank 1\n(6, 2, 'Foxtrot Item', 950),-- Rank 2\n(7, 2, 'Golf Item', 800);   -- Rank 3\n",
    "starterSql": "-- DoorDash: Find exactly 3-highest orders_fulfilled per borough\n-- Output: borough_name, merchant_name, orders_fulfilled\nWITH ranked AS (\n  -- Your code here\n)\nSELECT * FROM ranked;\n",
    "referenceSql": "WITH ranked AS (\n  SELECT \n    e.name AS borough_name,\n    i.name AS merchant_name,\n    i.orders_fulfilled,\n    DENSE_RANK() OVER (\n      PARTITION BY i.borough_id \n      ORDER BY i.orders_fulfilled DESC\n    ) AS rnk\n  FROM merchants i\n  JOIN boroughs e ON i.borough_id = e.id\n)\nSELECT \n  borough_name,\n  merchant_name,\n  orders_fulfilled\nFROM ranked\nWHERE rnk = 3\nORDER BY borough_name ASC, orders_fulfilled DESC;",
