    "description": "### Business Context\nThe AWS Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) team monitors heartbeat telemetry. When an infrastructure component fails successive healthchecks (where `status = 'DOWN'`), those failure timestamps must be clustered into a single **uninterrupted outage window**.\n\nHeartbeats arrive once every minute. A continuous outage island occurs when consecutive `'DOWN'` heartbeats have a delta of exactly 1 minute (60 seconds).\n\n### Metric Formulas & Rules\n- Filter for records where `status = 'DOWN'`.\n- Cluster consecutive failure heartbeats into contiguous outage windows using Gaps & Islands.\n- Output columns: `instance_id`, `outage_start`, `outage_end`, `consecutive_minutes`.\n- Only report outages lasting **at least 2 consecutive minutes** (`consecutive_minutes >= 2`).\n- Sort by `instance_id` ASC, `outage_start` ASC.\n\n### Input Schema\n**heartbeats** table:\n- `id` (INT PRIMARY KEY)\n- `instance_id` (INT)\n- `status` (VARCHAR: 'UP', 'DOWN')\n- `ping_time` (TIMESTAMP)",
    "schemaSql": "\nCREATE TABLE heartbeats (\n  id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  instance_id INT,\n  status VARCHAR(10),\n  ping_time TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nINSERT INTO heartbeats VALUES\n(1, 101, 'UP',   '2024-06-01 10:00:00'),\n(2, 101, 'DOWN', '2024-06-01 10:01:00'), -- Outage 1 start\n(3, 101, 'DOWN', '2024-06-01 10:02:00'),\n(4, 101, 'DOWN', '2024-06-01 10:03:00'), -- Outage 1 end (3 mins)\n(5, 101, 'UP',   '2024-06-01 10:04:00'),\n(6, 101, 'DOWN', '2024-06-01 10:10:00'), -- Single ping (1 min -> Excluded)\n(7, 102, 'DOWN', '2024-06-01 11:00:00'), -- Outage 2 start\n(8, 102, 'DOWN', '2024-06-01 11:01:00'); -- Outage 2 end (2 mins)\n",
    "starterSql": "-- AWS: Cluster consecutive DOWN heartbeats into outage windows\n-- Output: instance_id, outage_start, outage_end, consecutive_minutes\nWITH down_pings AS (\n  -- Your code here\n)\nSELECT * FROM down_pings;\n",
    "referenceSql": "WITH down_pings AS (\n  SELECT \n    instance_id,\n    ping_time,\n    ping_time - (ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY instance_id ORDER BY ping_time ASC) * INTERVAL '1 minute') AS island_grp\n  FROM heartbeats\n  WHERE status = 'DOWN'\n)\nSELECT \n  instance_id,\n  MIN(ping_time) AS outage_start,\n  MAX(ping_time) AS outage_end,\n  COUNT(*)::INT AS consecutive_minutes\nFROM down_pings\nGROUP BY instance_id, island_grp\nHAVING COUNT(*) >= 2\nORDER BY instance_id ASC, outage_start ASC;",
